# admin build-context dockerignore.
#
# BuildKit (enabled via `# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.7` in admin.Dockerfile)
# resolves a per-Dockerfile ignore file at <context>/<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore.
# The build context is the repo root and the Dockerfile is
# infra/docker/admin.Dockerfile, so this file MUST live at
# infra/docker/admin.Dockerfile.dockerignore for Docker to honor it (T-118-03).
# (The former infra/docker/.dockerignore.web matched none of Docker's lookup rules
# and was silently ignored — WR-01.)

# Local dependency installs (node_modules will be reinstalled inside the build container)
node_modules/
apps/admin/node_modules/
apps/client/node_modules/
packages/*/node_modules/

# Existing dist output (built inside the container, not from the host)
apps/admin/dist/
apps/client/dist/

# Backend source (not needed for frontend builds)
apps/backend/

# Test and tooling artifacts
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/coverage/
**/htmlcov/
**/.coverage

# Git and editor metadata
.git/
.gitignore
**/.gitkeep

# Planning and docs
.planning/
*.md
CLAUDE.md
**/CLAUDE.md

# Environment files (never in build context — T-118-03)
**/.env*

# TypeScript build info (stale artifacts)
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Design assets (not needed for production builds)
apps/admin/design/
apps/client/plans/
